WEBVTT

00:07.360 --> 00:09.110
<i>As a promise exchanged by their parents,</i>

00:09.110 --> 00:15.950
<i>the witch Nico and the ogre Morihito
had to suddenly begin living together.</i>

00:16.120 --> 00:19.240
<i>The high school life she was
looking forward to has been enriching,</i>

00:19.240 --> 00:22.500
<i>and in the midst of her feelings
toward Morihito on the rise,</i>

00:22.500 --> 00:25.170
<i>the tengu Kanshi also begins
living with them.</i>

00:26.670 --> 00:28.880
<i>Thanks to Kanshi's
high communication skills,</i>

00:29.040 --> 00:33.670
<i>the witch and her familiars' daily lives
continue to become livelier than ever.</i>

00:37.550 --> 00:39.260
Absolutely not!

00:39.430 --> 00:42.890
Please, I beg of you, Governor!

00:43.230 --> 00:46.480
You just have to wait one month
until I can pay my living expenses!

00:46.480 --> 00:47.770
No! I refuse!

00:47.980 --> 00:50.940
It's your fault for always blowing away
your allowance on useless things!

00:50.940 --> 00:52.570
Just pay with your body!

00:52.780 --> 00:53.650
What?

00:55.570 --> 01:01.450
AKEBONO PARK
NOW HIRING PERFORMERS
YOU CAN BE A FIGHTER
IN A HERO SHOW!

00:55.860 --> 00:59.330
They're hiring at Akebono Park
for their hero show.

00:59.830 --> 01:01.450
Now go work that body!

01:02.580 --> 01:06.670
I hate part-time jobs!
I don't wanna work!

01:06.670 --> 01:08.630
It's all troublesome and not fun at all,

01:08.630 --> 01:12.130
plus I feel myself becoming an adult
and it makes me sad!

01:12.130 --> 01:14.300
No! It's sad!

01:14.300 --> 01:16.840
Kanshi has the potential
to become a Super Neet.

02:48.560 --> 02:53.310
KANSHI'S PART-TIME JOB DIARIES
~THE SUPERHERO SHOW~

02:58.240 --> 03:01.910
Your acrobatic skills
are definitely top notch. You pass.

03:03.660 --> 03:06.240
I'm not even using half of my skills yet.

03:06.240 --> 03:09.460
Yeah, you might even be fit for that role.

03:10.370 --> 03:14.000
We originally had you come in
to try out for one of the fighter roles.

03:14.000 --> 03:17.800
But our actor for the hero suddenly
got injured, and can't play his role anymore.

03:19.130 --> 03:20.550
I'd like to ask you...

03:21.510 --> 03:23.550
to play the hero!

03:23.550 --> 03:25.180
Are you serious?

03:27.770 --> 03:31.770
Oh, nice!
You're looking good, Otto-man!

03:31.770 --> 03:35.310
He's called Otto-man?
I've never heard of him.

03:35.310 --> 03:37.530
You've never heard of Otto-man?

03:37.530 --> 03:40.690
It's quite a famous hero TV show
that's popular among moms and kids.

03:37.530 --> 03:41.990
MARRIED MAN
OTTO-MAN

03:40.690 --> 03:42.610
But not the dads?

03:43.860 --> 03:46.410
All right, let's get to rehearsing!

03:46.410 --> 03:49.450
We don't have that much time,
so just memorize the flow of things!

03:49.450 --> 03:51.330
Then we hit the stage in two hours!

03:51.330 --> 03:52.460
Yessir.

03:52.460 --> 03:54.750
My first job is pretty hard.

03:54.750 --> 03:57.210
Let's start with the first scene,
which is before he transforms.

03:57.590 --> 04:00.170
You come in when he transforms,
so just stand back and watch.

04:00.170 --> 04:01.550
All right.

04:01.550 --> 04:04.550
Let's start from the top,
all in one go. Action!

04:10.560 --> 04:15.270
<i>Otto-man, or rather, Yuichiro Sugata,
wakes up at 7am every morning.</i>

04:16.440 --> 04:17.860
Oh, good morning.

04:31.330 --> 04:35.500
<i>A high pressure front will bring sunny skies
to the Tokai and Kanto regions.</i>

04:35.500 --> 04:38.920
<i>However, the temperature seems
to be dropping for Western Japan.</i>

04:38.920 --> 04:43.220
<i>Kyushu will start to see some rain
early in the morning. And in...</i>

04:40.840 --> 04:43.220
<i>He doesn't really talk to his wife.</i>

04:43.220 --> 04:45.840
What the hell is this?
What am I watching right now?

04:45.840 --> 04:47.600
Hey, don't interrupt!

04:47.600 --> 04:50.010
This isn't something
you'd show at an amusement park!

04:50.010 --> 04:52.180
You obviously
have to start with the daily life!

04:52.180 --> 04:54.890
You definitely don't need the awkward
morning scene with the wife!

04:54.890 --> 04:56.270
This is what's important!

04:56.600 --> 04:58.980
You're new here,
so stop commenting on the scene!

04:58.980 --> 05:00.570
Okay, next! Commuting scene!

05:00.570 --> 05:02.530
This is the most boring hero show ever!

05:03.820 --> 05:08.490
<i>Since Otto-man wanted to sit down
on a seat, he let one train go by.</i>

05:08.490 --> 05:10.160
Do we really need this scene?

05:13.040 --> 05:14.660
So he couldn't sit after all?

05:15.500 --> 05:18.750
<i>At his temporary relocation, Otto-man
became friends with a lady coworker,</i>

05:18.750 --> 05:21.210
<i>Hanaoka, who invites him out to lunch.</i>

05:21.210 --> 05:23.130
When's the monster gonna come out?

05:23.420 --> 05:27.050
I'm sorry I had to decline your offer,
after you kindly invited me.

05:27.430 --> 05:28.970
But, why me?

05:28.970 --> 05:30.800
Oh, there you go again.

05:31.180 --> 05:35.730
"Why me, why me?" You always say that.

05:36.270 --> 05:39.900
I know so many good parts
about you, Mr. Sugata.

05:40.190 --> 05:44.360
It's only been a short time,
but I've always been watching you.

05:45.820 --> 05:48.320
Damn it, I think I'm getting
invested in this!

05:48.610 --> 05:52.660
I'm sorry, Mr. Sugata,
I know you're married and everything.

05:52.660 --> 05:56.580
But your short term here with us
is almost over, so I wanted to be brave.

05:57.500 --> 06:00.170
This isn't fair at all, is it?

06:00.170 --> 06:02.960
Man, who cares about the monsters,
what's gonna happen?

06:04.420 --> 06:06.970
I'm not sure how to answer.

06:06.970 --> 06:09.970
What's up with him?
You gotta be brave too, Otto-man!

06:10.340 --> 06:12.390
You're always dodging me, aren't you?

06:12.390 --> 06:14.680
Yeah, you tell him, Ms. Hanaoka!

06:14.680 --> 06:15.680
Mr. Sugata.

06:16.230 --> 06:17.390
No...

06:17.560 --> 06:18.520
Otto-man!

06:18.520 --> 06:19.650
Wait, what?!

06:19.650 --> 06:23.150
Are you serious?
It was Ms. Hanaoka all along?

06:23.150 --> 06:25.570
This time I'll meta-meta mess you up!

06:25.570 --> 06:27.400
There you are, you black company!

06:27.400 --> 06:29.530
You sure switched into fighting mode fast!

06:29.700 --> 06:30.910
You're up!

06:31.030 --> 06:33.990
You're Otto-man! Get out there and fight!

06:33.990 --> 06:36.290
I'm gonna go crazy!

06:37.040 --> 06:40.750
Working Man's Kick!

06:40.750 --> 06:43.170
Cut!

06:43.500 --> 06:45.590
Metaboli can't move around much
because of his size,

06:45.590 --> 06:47.460
so he's a villain who just gives orders!

06:47.460 --> 06:50.510
You're supposed to fight
these strestlers over here!

06:50.930 --> 06:52.180
Got it.

06:58.520 --> 07:01.900
At least the new guy
can move around really well.

07:02.350 --> 07:05.270
Okay, once you defeat them,
get back to work!

07:05.270 --> 07:06.780
Lunch time is almost over!

07:06.780 --> 07:08.400
You have to be that realistic?

07:09.530 --> 07:11.700
<i>And then, since he was late
returning from lunch,</i>

07:11.700 --> 07:14.870
<i>Otto-man received a stern lecture
from his manager for about an hour.</i>

07:14.870 --> 07:16.910
That's just way too sad.

07:19.250 --> 07:20.540
I'm home.

07:21.750 --> 07:25.540
Oh, you bought some wine?
Is there a special occasion?

07:26.380 --> 07:29.010
Yes, it's our wedding anniversary.

07:33.090 --> 07:35.300
The scenes at the house are so depressing.

07:35.890 --> 07:38.640
What? Did you forget?

07:38.640 --> 07:40.680
I-I'm so sorry.

07:41.020 --> 07:45.690
It looks like we'll have to do
that thing again then, won't we?

07:47.480 --> 07:48.360
Okay.

07:52.110 --> 07:57.280
<i>And so, Otto-man once again
becomes his wife's ottoman!</i>

07:57.280 --> 08:01.370
Ugh, your back is just the best for my feet.

08:02.000 --> 08:04.170
Otto-man, what are you doing, my man?!

08:04.170 --> 08:05.540
And, signature line!

08:05.540 --> 08:08.170
I! Am! Otto-man! Yeah!

08:08.170 --> 08:10.010
God damn it!

08:10.010 --> 08:12.300
You're so noisy about everything!

08:12.300 --> 08:14.970
By day, he's Otto-man,
and by night, he's an ottoman!

08:14.970 --> 08:17.180
I know why this isn't popular
among the dads!

08:17.180 --> 08:19.100
It's fine as long as the kids like it!

08:19.100 --> 08:21.480
You can't let children see this!

08:21.480 --> 08:25.100
Whatever, just don't disrupt
the performance on the stage.

08:25.100 --> 08:28.610
Follow the script, or you won't get paid!

08:29.190 --> 08:31.320
The real world sure is tough.

08:31.320 --> 08:33.650
Okay, everyone take a break
until the show starts.

08:46.080 --> 08:48.090
Are you the person who plays Metaboli?

08:48.960 --> 08:50.630
Your foot's injured.

08:51.010 --> 08:54.840
Yeah, I'm Hironaka, the guy
who used to play Otto-man.

08:55.130 --> 08:57.010
Sorry for causing you trouble.

08:57.800 --> 09:00.220
I sprained my ankle during rehearsal.

09:00.220 --> 09:02.890
I couldn't do stunts anymore,
so they switched me around.

09:03.390 --> 09:06.770
And my son was so excited because
it was my first hero role, too.

09:07.440 --> 09:10.070
I really let him down.

09:10.980 --> 09:15.150
I'm sorry to hear that.
Is your son here today?

09:15.530 --> 09:18.280
Yeah, he'd already bought a ticket.

09:18.780 --> 09:23.330
So I'll have to do my best
when playing as Metaboli.

09:26.370 --> 09:29.460
It's tough when your parent
has to break a promise.

09:29.710 --> 09:32.090
It feels like you saw a weak part of them.

09:32.630 --> 09:36.930
Especially for my dad. I want him to be
this unwavering, strong presence.

09:40.850 --> 09:43.850
Mr. Hironaka, can you contact your son?

09:43.850 --> 09:44.810
What?

09:46.230 --> 09:48.650
Tell him, "I! Am! Otto-man!"

09:58.990 --> 10:00.570
<i>And then, it was showtime.</i>

10:01.530 --> 10:02.620
That's kinda weird.

10:02.620 --> 10:05.410
How dare you do this to me!

10:05.410 --> 10:07.960
I'm gonna meta-meta mess you up so fast!

10:08.290 --> 10:10.130
Something feels off.

10:10.130 --> 10:11.670
This wasn't in the script!

10:11.670 --> 10:14.760
Try to punch me, you super-masochist
foot rest! I'll take you out in no time!

10:14.760 --> 10:16.970
Metaboli isn't that spirited!

10:17.170 --> 10:19.550
That monster is Kan, right?

10:19.550 --> 10:22.010
But he told us he'd be playing the hero.

10:22.010 --> 10:23.470
Maybe something came up.

10:23.890 --> 10:26.100
Uh, hey, Kanshi.
What am I supposed to do?

10:26.100 --> 10:27.140
Come at me!

10:27.140 --> 10:28.390
But my ankle...

10:28.390 --> 10:30.230
Whatever you can manage is fine!

10:30.690 --> 10:33.520
A son's first hero is his father.

10:33.520 --> 10:35.860
You have to show him your strength!

10:42.830 --> 10:43.870
Cushion kick.

10:51.790 --> 10:53.460
What?!

10:55.590 --> 10:57.210
Otto-man's strong!

10:57.550 --> 10:58.970
K-Kanshi, are you okay?

10:58.970 --> 11:02.760
What the hell's up with this guy?
He's way stronger than I thought. I'm scared!

11:02.760 --> 11:06.220
I'll get you, you little brat!
Come at me, Otto-man!

11:06.640 --> 11:07.730
Cushion punch.

11:06.810 --> 11:07.730
BOOP

11:09.190 --> 11:10.230
<i>And on today's show,</i>

11:10.690 --> 11:14.480
<i>the super-strong Otto-man defeated
the monster with flashy action!</i>

11:14.730 --> 11:17.230
<i>It was said to be
the most successful show yet.</i>

11:17.230 --> 11:19.110
This feels too good!

11:24.030 --> 11:26.330
Switching roles and ignoring the script!

11:26.330 --> 11:28.540
How could you do such a thing?

11:28.700 --> 11:30.620
No paychecks for the both of you!

11:31.750 --> 11:34.540
<i>From today's work shift,
Kanshi Kazamatsuri made...</i>

11:35.040 --> 11:36.210
<i>zero yen.</i>

11:37.510 --> 11:39.920
I don't think I'm cut out for part-time work.

11:42.010 --> 11:45.930
But I think your personality
would be great in a work environment.

11:46.430 --> 11:49.890
I think it'll be a good idea
to keep trying different kinds of jobs.

11:49.890 --> 11:50.980
What?

11:50.980 --> 11:52.940
I'll wait
for this month's living expenses.

11:53.060 --> 11:56.650
Really? Hey, what's gotten into you
all of a sudden? So nice!

11:56.650 --> 11:59.150
Moi is actually a nice person, Kan.

11:59.320 --> 12:02.280
Hey, after a month passes,
you'll just be paying two month's worth.

12:02.570 --> 12:04.700
If you can't pay up, you'll get punished.

12:04.910 --> 12:08.580
I know, I get it! I promise
I won't waste any more money!

12:11.160 --> 12:12.620
Isn't that nice?

12:15.540 --> 12:18.050
I! Am! Otto-man! Yeah!

12:22.680 --> 12:24.050
<i>One month later...</i>

12:41.490 --> 12:46.990
WAITING 30 MINUTES
UNTIL THE INSTANT NOODLES ARE DONE.
"MY CELL PHONE IS SO SLOW, TOO."

12:47.530 --> 12:53.370
KANSHI'S PART-TIME JOB DIARIES
~THE SIDE JOB~

13:21.860 --> 13:22.900
<i>My side job...</i>

13:23.650 --> 13:25.950
<i>is going to make my brain melt.</i>

13:26.860 --> 13:29.160
I can't do this anymore!

13:29.160 --> 13:33.080
I picked up a side job of packing screws
to make some money, but I hate it!

13:33.080 --> 13:34.660
I want to quit!

13:34.910 --> 13:39.000
I haven't even gone through one box,
and I'm already sick of looking at screws.

13:39.000 --> 13:43.050
But I need to make money during break time
or I won't be able to pay the living expenses.

13:43.170 --> 13:47.180
I really don't want to be Otto-man anymore!

13:47.760 --> 13:49.930
A spell that makes you move faster?

13:50.140 --> 13:51.510
Please, Nico.

13:51.510 --> 13:53.140
There is one, but why do you need it?

13:53.140 --> 13:56.890
Your movements are already
so fidgety that you're restless.

13:56.890 --> 13:58.060
That's kinda rude.

13:58.060 --> 13:59.940
I'm not progressing with my side job.

13:59.940 --> 14:01.570
I thought about working
while watching a movie,

14:01.570 --> 14:04.150
but from the start of the movie
to the end, I'm still holding the same screw.

14:04.150 --> 14:06.570
- Isn't that weird?
- That's because you're watching the movie.

14:06.740 --> 14:08.530
And I took on a large quantity, too.

14:08.530 --> 14:11.700
My room is packed with boxes
and I'll never finish!

14:12.410 --> 14:15.450
I can speed you up to 1.5 times faster
all the way to 10 times faster.

14:15.450 --> 14:18.460
The faster the better.
I'll take the maximum speed, please!

14:18.460 --> 14:20.380
It comes with a lot of warnings, though.

14:20.380 --> 14:23.250
If you just tell me what they are,
I'll be careful.

14:23.250 --> 14:26.470
I feel like I'm watching an old man buy
an appliance that he doesn't know much about.

14:26.630 --> 14:28.550
Okay, here are the warnings.

14:28.550 --> 14:30.720
One. This spell cannot be dispelled
at any point.

14:30.720 --> 14:33.180
The effect will wear off automatically
in three days' time.

14:33.180 --> 14:36.060
That's great.
I can concentrate on my side job.

14:36.060 --> 14:39.600
Two. While under this spell,
you cannot attack anything.

14:39.940 --> 14:43.860
What an absurd thing to say.
I'm just gonna be putting screws in bags.

14:43.860 --> 14:47.490
Three. You might have a mental breakdown
for the 10 times faster option.

14:47.490 --> 14:49.490
What does that even mean?

14:49.610 --> 14:53.620
That's just complaints from normies
who can't handle speed, right?

14:53.620 --> 14:56.080
I'm a speedster tengu!

14:56.080 --> 14:57.710
<i>Kanshi Kazamatsuri...</i>

14:57.710 --> 14:59.290
Go ahead, Nico.

14:59.460 --> 15:03.710
<i>...is the type of person who'll act first
without thinking, and then regret it later.</i>

15:03.710 --> 15:05.130
Okay, here we go.

15:05.380 --> 15:07.970
Kwi-kwick, 10 times speed!

15:09.840 --> 15:11.930
How is it, Kan?

15:17.890 --> 15:19.850
Did he say, "Ree"? What?

15:19.850 --> 15:20.900
Kan?

15:24.150 --> 15:27.690
Oh no, Kan's just saying, "Ree ree rah."

15:27.690 --> 15:30.860
H-He's moving so fast
that we can't understand him.

15:32.490 --> 15:34.990
He got a piece of paper
and is writing something down.

15:34.990 --> 15:36.790
He decided that talking won't work.

15:36.910 --> 15:39.910
I CAN'T UNDERSTAND
WHAT YOU GUYS ARE SAYING.

15:39.120 --> 15:39.910
What?

15:40.160 --> 15:44.250
I get it! His brain is moving
at 10 times the speed.

15:44.840 --> 15:46.590
From Kanshi's point of view,

15:46.590 --> 15:50.550
we're moving at 0.1 times the speed,
so our words are also slowing down, too.

15:51.010 --> 15:54.800
What kind of world is that?

16:04.810 --> 16:08.320
They're speaking in a low tone
and sound just like ghosts! Super scary!

16:08.820 --> 16:13.700
And their movements are slow the entire time
and it's rattling my brain. Way too horror!

16:16.410 --> 16:18.080
Please stop that!

16:18.080 --> 16:21.330
I'm gonna go insane!
When is this gonna be over?

16:21.750 --> 16:24.330
<i>One. The effect will wear off automatically
in three days' time.</i>

16:25.040 --> 16:26.500
That's right.

16:26.880 --> 16:30.840
I can't. I can't be around them anymore.

16:31.420 --> 16:32.930
I'll just get to work.

17:02.830 --> 17:04.210
This still sucks.

17:05.210 --> 17:06.920
What the hell?

17:06.920 --> 17:10.130
I thought I'd be moving 10 times faster
so I can finish, but that's not the case.

17:10.340 --> 17:11.840
Time is moving slower!

17:11.840 --> 17:14.760
It's only been ten minutes?
I've been at this for almost two hours!

17:15.800 --> 17:20.470
I can't talk to anyone,
so is this loneliness going to last for three days?

17:22.140 --> 17:25.900
<i>It's not three days. It's 30 days.</i>

17:26.150 --> 17:29.150
You're kidding me, right?
I have to be by myself for a month?

17:29.150 --> 17:31.650
No, no! I can't do it!

17:31.650 --> 17:34.780
I have to tell Nico, and ask her
to get me back to normal.

17:37.070 --> 17:38.120
He's back.

17:38.120 --> 17:40.160
It's only been ten minutes.

17:41.290 --> 17:42.160
He's saying something.

17:42.500 --> 17:44.540
We can't understand you.

17:44.540 --> 17:47.170
Kanshi, slower. Try talking slower.

17:44.540 --> 17:47.170
TALK SLOWER

17:48.710 --> 17:49.420
Slower.

17:50.750 --> 17:51.920
More slower.

17:52.630 --> 17:54.380
I'm sad.

17:54.380 --> 17:55.630
You're sad, huh?

17:55.630 --> 17:59.510
I'm sorry, Kan!
I can't do anything about this.

17:59.510 --> 18:01.430
Nico, he can't understand you.

18:04.140 --> 18:05.730
I can't do anything about this!

18:05.730 --> 18:07.190
That might work.

18:12.900 --> 18:15.860
There he goes. This really is kinda sad.

18:16.320 --> 18:17.700
Wait, there he is.

18:18.610 --> 18:19.950
He's eating.

18:20.450 --> 18:24.580
Wait a minute. In Kanshi's world,
since everything is sped up by ten,

18:25.120 --> 18:27.710
that means he'll probably eat
30 meals in one day!

18:27.710 --> 18:28.920
What?

18:29.460 --> 18:32.250
He finished eating within seconds
and went back to his room.

18:32.630 --> 18:35.760
I feel so sorry for him
that I can't watch anymore.

18:37.840 --> 18:41.350
So for three days,
we won't be able to talk to him,

18:41.640 --> 18:44.350
and he'll be running through the house
over and over.

18:44.350 --> 18:45.600
Yeah.

18:45.980 --> 18:50.400
But let's just try to be sympathetic toward
the lonely struggle that he's going through.

18:50.940 --> 18:55.280
I did say three days,
but for Kan, it might be...

18:55.480 --> 18:56.860
Don't think about that.

18:57.360 --> 18:58.490
There he is again.

18:58.490 --> 18:59.660
What is it now?

18:59.990 --> 19:01.530
He's eating again.

19:01.740 --> 19:04.240
What? But he just ate 30 minutes ago.

19:04.370 --> 19:07.410
Thirty minutes times ten is around
five hours, so it wouldn't be strange.

19:07.410 --> 19:09.540
That's just so sad.

19:10.210 --> 19:14.710
Kan is the one who loved talking
while eating with everyone the most, too.

19:14.710 --> 19:17.300
Now he's just speedily
eating his food, then leaving.

19:17.510 --> 19:21.550
I'm sorry, Kan, you must be so lonely.
I'll try to be nice.

19:23.510 --> 19:25.060
Please stop freaking me out!

19:26.140 --> 19:27.310
He said something.

19:28.100 --> 19:32.060
<i>And so, Kanshi's lifestyle speed
times ten continued.</i>

19:32.690 --> 19:36.530
<i>For now, we purchased more food
and placed it on the dining room table.</i>

19:36.980 --> 19:40.400
<i>We're not sure when he's eating it,
but it's been decreasing at a fast pace.</i>

19:41.240 --> 19:43.320
<i>When we pass by each other
in the house,</i>

19:43.660 --> 19:47.330
<i>he'll stop in front of me
for a split second, and then leave.</i>

19:48.120 --> 19:50.620
<i>But for him,
it probably wasn't a split second.</i>

19:51.580 --> 19:53.830
<i>I become ashamed of my slowness.</i>

19:54.790 --> 19:57.090
<i>At night, I peeked into his room.</i>

19:57.800 --> 19:59.840
<i>He had long since finished his part-time job</i>

20:00.380 --> 20:03.090
<i>and was staring quietly
at his household shrine.</i>

20:04.010 --> 20:05.930
<i>I closed the door.</i>

20:08.430 --> 20:10.730
<i>When I woke up in the morning,
there was a message.</i>

20:08.430 --> 20:10.730
ONE DAY IS REALLY LONG.
IT'S REALLY TIRESOME.
I KNOW.
CAN YOU PLEASE BUY ME UNDERWEAR?

20:11.520 --> 20:14.360
<i>For him, several days had already passed.</i>

20:14.610 --> 20:16.610
<i>Looks like he's washing
his underwear by hand.</i>

20:17.440 --> 20:19.190
<i>But it's taking forever to dry.</i>

20:19.570 --> 20:22.110
<i>All the underwear he owned
was gently swaying in the wind.</i>

20:22.570 --> 20:24.110
<i>I ran out and bought more underwear.</i>

20:24.490 --> 20:26.620
<i>He then appeared in front of me
like the wind.</i>

20:27.120 --> 20:31.370
<i>He grasped my hand,
and cried for about three seconds.</i>

20:34.710 --> 20:37.130
Thanks for coming, Keigo.

20:38.090 --> 20:39.260
Kamaitachi weasel?

20:39.260 --> 20:40.380
It's Kan.

20:40.710 --> 20:42.840
Oh, yeah, that's right.

20:43.930 --> 20:47.050
So you said you had an idea?

20:47.140 --> 20:48.140
Yeah.

20:48.140 --> 20:51.770
There's an app where you can record his voice
and then replay it at a slower speed.

20:52.600 --> 20:55.520
I see. Then we can hear what he's saying.

20:55.520 --> 20:59.280
Oh, Kan.
You'll finally be able to talk to us.

20:59.530 --> 21:01.110
It's been two days.

21:01.110 --> 21:03.900
For him, he hasn't had a decent conversation
with anyone for 20 days.

21:05.870 --> 21:07.240
- Kanshi?
- Kan?

21:10.870 --> 21:13.290
How are you guys?

21:13.540 --> 21:14.580
He talked!

21:14.580 --> 21:16.920
I didn't even record him yet,
but he's talking normally.

21:17.130 --> 21:21.710
I... prac... ticed.

21:22.090 --> 21:24.970
I practiced!

21:24.970 --> 21:28.800
<i>With a lot of time on his hands,
Kanshi had mastered the Slow Language.</i>

21:29.890 --> 21:31.810
<i>And we all hung out together.</i>

21:32.430 --> 21:34.690
I even practiced walking, too.

21:34.940 --> 21:38.940
It's hard to walk slowly,
so you just gotta take smaller steps.

21:39.400 --> 21:40.730
This is how I walk.

21:39.980 --> 21:41.820
SCOOT
SCOOT
SCOOT

21:40.730 --> 21:41.820
Scary!

21:43.190 --> 21:46.200
<i>That night, we all ate together
at the dinner table.</i>

21:47.160 --> 21:50.580
<i>The rice I put in his bowl
disappeared in an instant,</i>

21:51.370 --> 21:53.160
<i>but he still sat with us.</i>

21:57.420 --> 22:00.340
<i>Just when he was getting used
to that slow life,</i>

22:00.590 --> 22:01.960
<i>the time had finally come.</i>

22:01.960 --> 22:04.470
It made me laugh so hard.

22:07.180 --> 22:08.340
It's back to normal.

22:08.510 --> 22:09.390
You did it, Kanshi.

22:09.390 --> 22:10.850
Welcome back, Kan.

22:12.350 --> 22:15.480
You guys are talking way too fast

22:15.480 --> 22:17.810
and it's scary!

22:17.810 --> 22:19.610
Why are you talking like that?

22:19.980 --> 22:23.780
<i>Kanshi was now being afflicted
with speed lag!</i>

22:23.940 --> 22:25.570
I'm gonna go insane!

23:57.580 --> 24:00.620
Let's do the next episode preview
with two times the speed. Kwi-kwick!

24:00.620 --> 24:02.290
How was this episode's WITCH WATCH?
Man, I really had a rough time.

24:02.290 --> 24:03.540
Before that, hurry up
and buy me new underwear.

24:03.540 --> 24:04.460
So I can replace the ones you wore!

24:04.460 --> 24:05.840
I wore it by mistake!
I washed it and gave it back.

24:05.840 --> 24:07.760
Washing it won't cut it! If your crotch
touches it once, I can never wear it again.

24:06.750 --> 24:11.970
NEXT EPISODE
DEAR KARA
NEW FRIENDS
DATE WITH THE KNIGHT

24:07.760 --> 24:09.800
How could you say that?
I thought we were friends.

24:09.800 --> 24:11.970
- You wore ogre underwear but you're still weak.
- What are you guys even talking about?
